  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#crossorigingetownpropertyhelper-(-o,-p-) step 2 says:\r\n\r\n> Let crossOriginKey be a tuple consisting of the current settings object's origin's effective domain, O's relevant settings object's origin's effective domain, and P.\r\n\r\nand then this key is later used for lookups into the map.  Consider a page at http://foo.com that loads subframes from http://bar.com and http://bar.com:8000.  These two subframes both try to access `parent.close`.  In both cases, \"current settings object's origin's effective domain\" is \"bar.com\" and \"relevant settings object's origin's effective domain\" is \"foo.com\", so per spec as currently written they must see the same function object.  I'm pretty sure this is not right.  ;)",
